    ...text(r'''Rust makes you import everything. Every Vec is in the prelude, but HashMap, Arc, io::Error, a serde derive, a trait you need in scope to call a method: each is a trip to the top of the file, or a trip to the code action menu. rust-analyzer will do the typing for you with Import `std::collections::HashMap`, but you have to stop, open the menu and pick. When there is exactly one candidate that is a wasted round trip. When there are several, this plugin ranks them by what the project already does instead of leaving the server’s order.'''),
